## Open Source Usage Guidelines

### Getting Started
1. Fork this repository to your own GitHub account
2. Clone your fork locally: `git clone https://github.com/your-username/life-dashboard.git`
3. Install dependencies: `./setup.sh`
4. Configure your credentials in `backend/.env` (see README.md for details)
5. Run the application: `./start.sh`
6. Access at: http://localhost:3000

### Contributing
We welcome contributions! Please:
1. Fork the repository
2. Create a feature branch: `git checkout -b feature/amazing-feature`
3. Commit your changes: `git commit -m 'Add amazing feature'`
4. Push to the branch: `git push origin feature/amazing-feature`
5. Open a pull request

### Security Note
For security reasons, never commit your `.env` file containing API keys and tokens.
This repository includes a `.gitignore` file to prevent accidental commits of sensitive data.
Always keep your credentials private and environment-specific.

### Customization
Feel free to modify this dashboard to suit your needs:
- Add additional service integrations (Slack, Trello, Todoist, etc.)
- Customize the urgency scoring algorithm
- Modify the UI/theme to match your preferences
- Extend functionality with new features

